WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.674
Hi! Today we're going to meet really big numbers, all the way up to ten million!

2
00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:11.730
Imagine a big stadium with 50 000 seats.

3
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:20.250
One hundred stadiums like that have 5 000 000 seats altogether! How do we read and write such a big number?

4
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:30.882
We use a place value chart. From right to left: ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, and millions.

5
00:00:31.032 --> 00:00:39.786
Let's put 4 352 018 into the chart. The 4 is in the millions place, so it stands for 4 000 000.

6
00:00:39.936 --> 00:00:46.770
In English, we read it in groups of three: four million, three hundred and fifty-two thousand and eighteen.

7
00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:56.010
When we write it, we leave a space every three digits from the right: 4 352 018. Now it is easy to read.

8
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:05.514
Add 1 to 9 999 999 and you get ten million. That is a 1 followed by seven zeros.

9
00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:11.130
Let's write this number in numerals: three million, five thousand and sixty.

10
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:17.154
Put 3 in the millions place, 5 in the thousands place, and 6 in the tens place.

11
00:01:17.304 --> 00:01:25.770
Every empty place gets a zero. So the number is 3 005 060.

12
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:32.346
One more: in 2 704 315, what is the value of the digit 7?

13
00:01:32.496 --> 00:01:42.594
Count from the right: ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands. The 7 is in the hundred thousands place.

14
00:01:42.744 --> 00:01:48.762
So its value is 700 000, seven hundred thousand.

15
00:01:48.912 --> 00:01:55.650
Watch out! Some pupils write only the digits they hear, and get 35 060.

16
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:04.242
But some places are empty, and they need zeros. The correct answer is 3 005 060.

17
00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:11.322
When you finish, count the digits. A number in the millions has 7 digits.

18
00:02:11.472 --> 00:02:22.026
Your turn! Write in numerals: six million, forty thousand and three hundred. Pause and think.

19
00:02:22.176 --> 00:02:29.802
The answer is 6 040 300. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:29.952 --> 00:02:41.106
Another one! What is the value of the digit 9 in 5 093 610? Pause and think.

21
00:02:41.256 --> 00:02:48.978
The 9 is in the ten thousands place, so its value is 90 000. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:49.128 --> 00:02:59.898
Last one! What is the value of the digit 4 in 3 461 200? Pause and think.

23
00:03:00.048 --> 00:03:08.322
The 4 is in the hundred thousands place, so its value is 400 000. Did you get it right?

24
00:03:08.472 --> 00:03:16.146
Remember: use a place value chart, put zeros in the empty places, and leave a space every three digits.

25
00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:20.490
Now go and practise in your garden!

